SM-T715 tablet: the voice bar in other languages than English.

Upstream's voice bar (omamobile.voice, shipped again by 0004) is English
only: its settings offer Whisper's tiny.en, base.en and small.en,
omamobile-voice-preview hard-codes language "en" and the .en models, and
omamobile-setup-user sets Voxtype up only when omamobile-voice ships
ggml-base.en.bin. The tablet's session runs in French, and the tablet's
omamobile-voice ships Whisper's multilingual base (ggml-base.bin) instead.
- VoiceModel.js, Voice.qml: a Language choice at the top of the voice
  settings (Automatic, English, Français, Deutsch, Español, Italiano,
  Português, Nederlands), written to Voxtype's config ([whisper] language:
  auto, en, fr, ...) through Voxtype's own setter, key by key as upstream
  sets the model, so the user's other settings stay; the daemon restarts
  to load it. The speech models follow the language: English, the .en ones
  as upstream; any other language or Automatic, the multilingual tiny,
  base and small, as the same Fast, Balanced and Accurate rows. A new
  language takes the same size in the other family (downloaded through
  Voxtype first when it is not on disk), the language and the model set in
  the order that never leaves the daemon a model deaf to its language. A
  language set by hand that the list lacks shows as a row of its own.
- omamobile-voice-preview: its own config carries the configured language
  (no longer "en"), with a model that hears it: for English tiny.en, else
  the multilingual tiny, else the daemon's base.en or base; for any other
  language or auto, tiny, else the daemon's base; never a .en model.
- omamobile-setup-user: Voxtype is set up out of the box when ggml-base.bin
  or ggml-base.en.bin is in /usr/share/omamobile/voice/models (whichever
  are there are linked). The config that first setup creates hears the
  session's language: LC_ALL, then LC_MESSAGES, then LANG (then
  /etc/locale.conf's, for a run outside a session such as the image's
  build), its first two letters when the settings offer that language,
  else en; its model is base for another language than English when
  ggml-base.bin is shipped, base.en for English when ggml-base.en.bin is,
  and otherwise whichever is shipped, with the language that model hears
  (base.en: en). Only [whisper]'s model and language lines change (the two
  lines alone without Omarchy's config); a config the user has stays.
- Tests: test/voice-model.js, test/voice-preview.py and test/setup-user.sh
  (its run() passes the locale variables and a locale.conf) cover all of
  it; test/all's voice section checks the settings' wiring.
Against omarchy-mobile 8991845 (omamobile-shell 0.2.147), after 0001-0013.

